# What `railway up` must never upload.
#
# `railway up` sends the WORKING DIRECTORY, not a git ref, so anything sitting
# untracked in this tree ships to the API image. Two things made that expensive:
#
#   .claude/worktrees/ alone is ~193MB and holds a full nested copy of this repo,
#   so a deploy uploaded the source twice — and a nested worktree being written to
#   by another agent mid-upload is how a half-written file once shipped.
#
# .gitignore already covers node_modules/, dist/ and .env*. This file covers the
# untracked working material that .gitignore deliberately does not.
.claude/
.impeccable/
.superpowers/
.rollout-audit-backups/
.worktrees/

# Local scratch.
probe-tmp.mjs
*.local.mjs

# Documentation and QA evidence. Read by people, never by the running API.
docs/

# Test-only artifacts.
web/test-results/
web/playwright-report/
